# EigenScript #898: null is not a dict. Reading a field off a null-typed
# target used to answer null silently (optional-chaining through a miss);
# it now raises, and the AOT must raise in the same place with the same
# kind and message rather than answering and running on.
#
# The `_err` in the filename selects the harness's raising class: stdout
# before the death and the error message must match the VM exactly, while
# the VM-only source excerpt / caret / stack-trace lines are normalized
# away (see aot/test/run.sh — the AOT has no bytecode offset to site from).
#
# The index-side twin (`null["k"]` -> "cannot index null") is the same bug
# one layer over: aot_index_get was missing the oracle's final else, so it
# answered null for every unindexable target, not just this one. It cannot
# share this file — the first raise ends the program — so it lives in
# t61_null_index_err.eigs.

d is {"a": 1}
print of d.a
print of d.missing

# reachable: setting a field through null stays a silent no-op (#898
# changed the READ only — the AOT must not "symmetrize" this)
n is null
n.f is 3
print of "null-set is a no-op"

# and here the program dies
print of n.f
print of "UNREACHABLE — the VM stops above; an AOT that prints this is the bug"
